mories of  murdoch stored in it now all he has to  do is inject it in someone and they will  be able to track murdoch instantly as  everyone stares at him in confusion one  of the senior strangers mr hand emerges  from the crowd and agrees to volunteer  the leader mr book gives the heads up  and soon mr hand is injected with the  strange liquid after convulsing for a  while he finally wakes up with all the  memories of murdoch in the next scene  murdock reaches the subway in search of  shell beach he asks some people about  directions to the place but surprisingly  all of them have forgotten about it  confused he once again stares at the  greeting card and finds the name karl  harris written on it the initials of the  same name were inscribed on the suitcase  back at the hotel later murdoch tracks  down carl's address and visits his home  the old man reminisces about the past  where murdoch was a kid but as expected  he doesn't remember any of it just then  he gets curious and asks carl why it's  always night but the latter simply tells  him to take some rest after murdoch goes  to another room carl secretly calls emma  and informs her about murdoch's arrival  she in turn tells inspector bumstead and  proceeds to the location with him but  sadly mr hand who has been tracking emma  using murdock's memories overhears her  entire conversation when murdoch finds  out that carl has revealed his location  he tries to escape the place but it's  too late the strangers led by mr hand  have already arrived outside and they  start attacking murdoch however using  his extremely complex telekinetic powers  and the will to survive murdoch  continues evading them he somehow  manages to get onto the street but is  again surrounded by the strangers just  as he is about to be apprehended emma  and the inspector arrive in their car  and take him away the scene then cuts to  the police station where inspector  bumstead is interrogating murdoch as he  believes that he is behind the murders  however an agitated murdoch flips the  questions and instead asks the inspector  if he remembers the way to shell beach  as expected bumstead does know the place  but even he cannot seem to recall the  directions then murdock asks him why  they're always experiencing night and  why they have no memories of the day if  they have no memories of it how do they  know it's a thing he even makes a book  levitate to prove his point that they  are dealing with something supernatural  after a while some strangers led by mr  hand enter the police station and start  looking for murdoch they put all the  officers to sleep and head to the cell  however upon reaching it they find that  their target has already escaped in the  meantime murdoch confronts dr schreiber  at a bath house and demands answers he  wants to know what is going on in the  city and why the strangers are after him  the doctor calms them down and reveals  that they are all part of a grand  experiment that the strangers are  conducting just then inspector bumstead  arrives at the scene and takes control  of the doctor here it is revealed that  the inspector himself released murdoch  out of custody as he too wants to find  answers after that the inspector and  murdoch forced the doctor to lead them  to shell beach they get in a car and  start their journey but for some reason  the doctor keeps mentioning that going  there is of no use shortly after they  reach a dead end as a bridge has  mysteriously disappeared hence the three  decide to continue by boat during the  journey dr schrieber finally explains  everything that is happening with the  city he reveals that the strangers are  aliens from another planet and they came  to earth after they almost faced  extinction when they saw the human  population prospering they immediately  decided to emulate them however the  problem was that they didn't have any  souls and that is what differentiates  them from the humans adamant on saving  their race the strangers then created an  entire city abducted humans from  different parts of the world and placed  them there every night at 12 they stop  everyone and install new memories in  them so that they can compare the  different characteristics in humans the  plan is to know everything about the  human soul and become just like them dr  schrieber further mentions that he is  the best psychologist in town and this  is why the strangers don't erase his  memory every night murdoch then asks why  it's always night to which the doctor  replies that the strangers are afraid of  light so they created a city where it's  always dark after a while they arrive at  shell beach only to find that it's  merely a poster on a wall enraged  murdoch and inspector bumstead grab some  iron bars and begin striking the wall  the doctor begs the duo to stop but they  don't listen eventually they break the  wall and are taken aback to find endless  space on the other side this confirms  that the city is a mere experiment and  there will be no escaping it just then  mr hand and his henchmen arrive at the  scene with a captive emma and threaten  murdoch to surrender the inspector  immediately retaliates but he is thrown  out into the abyss before he dies he  witnesses the city floating in space  which is surrounded by nothing but  darkness here we get to know that this  city is just a huge spaceship on the  other hand mr hand uses emma as leverage  and eventually captures murdock in the  next scene murdoch is seen tied to a  chair as the entire stranger community  that's right the whole bald brigade  shouts for his death however their  leader mr book claims that he has other  ideas he summons dr schrieber and asks  him to inject murdock with an imprint  which will transfer his soul into all  the strangers hesitantly the doctor  obliges but instead of the imprint he  injects murdock with another syringe one  which contains all of his memories as  soon as it is administered all of  murdoch's memories flash 